@startuml
!include _libcpg-theme.iuml
title Martin package metrics and stable-dependency evidence

skinparam component {
  BackgroundColor #F1F3F5
  BorderColor #495057
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFF9DB
  BorderColor #F08C00
}

component "CodePropertyGraph" as CPG #DBE4FF
component "ModuleAssignment" as ASSIGN #FFE8CC
component "GraphProjection\nsource depends on target" as VIEW #C3FAE8
component "Cross-module sets" as SETS #D3F9D8
component "Type-declaration counts" as TYPES #E9ECEF
component "MartinMetrics" as METRICS #E5DBFF
component "SDP comparison" as SDP #FFF3BF
component "SdpViolation witnesses" as WITNESS #FFE3E3

CPG --> ASSIGN : Module ancestors / source path\n/ caller pairs
VIEW --> SETS : canonical edges\nweights ignored
ASSIGN --> SETS : <latex>\mu:V\rightharpoonup M</latex>
CPG --> TYPES : abstract Class + Trait\nover Class + Struct + Enum + Trait
ASSIGN --> TYPES : bucket each declaration

SETS --> METRICS : <latex>C_a, C_e, I=\frac{C_e}{C_a+C_e}</latex>
TYPES --> METRICS : <latex>A=\frac{N_a}{N_t}</latex>\n<latex>D=|A+I-1|</latex>
METRICS --> SDP : compare module-edge endpoints
VIEW --> SDP : retain concrete edge evidence
ASSIGN --> SDP : aggregate by module pair
SDP --> WITNESS : <latex>I(X) < I(Y)</latex>

note bottom of METRICS
  Lexical module order
  Feature-free and read-only
  All scalars in <latex>[0,1]</latex>
end note

note bottom of WITNESS
  One row per violating module pair
  smallest NodeId edge + dependency count
  advisory structural evidence
end note

legend bottom
|= Color |= Concept |
|<#DBE4FF>| CPG/type syntax evidence |
|<#FFE8CC>| explicit module boundary policy |
|<#C3FAE8>| directed dependency projection |
|<#D3F9D8>| coupling-set aggregation |
|<#E9ECEF>| abstraction counts |
|<#E5DBFF>| scalar metric report |
|<#FFF3BF>| Stable Dependencies Principle decision |
|<#FFE3E3>| concrete violation evidence |
endlegend
@enduml
